  "name": "Her Art Here – California",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "low",
  "drawnOn": "B752",
  "description": "Fuselage: White with California artwork low on the sides; white underside forward. Forward, from the nose to the engine: a band of light-blue breaking-wave texture along the lower fuselage, edged above by a royal-blue stripe (with a thin teal line under it) that rises from the bottom of the nose and runs aft just below the windows. Royal-blue mask round the cockpit windows. Over the wing: light-blue and dark palm trees above the windows. Aft: the Golden Gate Bridge in royal blue, a tower behind the wing and its cables across the windows, over royal-blue hills that rise from the belly behind the wing to fill the tail cone, a paler fog layer above them. Tail: Standard United blue fin with the light-blue globe. Engines: Royal-blue cowlings, polished lips. Winglets: Blue. Titles: Large, widely spaced royal-blue 'UNITED' over the forward windows. Artwork: Tsungwei Moo's California design.",
  "sources": [
