    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N14106_EWR_Landing_4R_UA_B757_224_Her_Art_Here_Tsungwei_Moo_California_Small_(53609851063).png",
      "title": "N14106 EWR Landing 4R UA B757 224 Her Art Here Tsungwei Moo California (CC BY-SA 2.0)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-12",
      "note": "Right side, level, 2024-03-25: the only openly licensed photo of the scheme found. Geometry mirrored from it. Strong blue-violet color cast (the same photographer's NY/NJ shot shows the same cast), so blues are matched to the NY/NJ aircraft's natural-color photos instead."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Drawn from a single right-side photo (2024-03-25) with a strong color cast; the left side wasn't seen in any openly licensed photo and is assumed to carry the same layout (as on the NY/NJ sister aircraft). Colors follow the NY/NJ aircraft's blues, so they are low confidence. History entry: in Amarillo for repaint Feb 2025; standard livery by Feb 2026. Re-checked 2026-11-15: no new photo; the wave's and the stripe's sweep up from the belly and the hills' rise into the tail cone drawn as curves (corners where the stripe's straight run starts and at its square aft end). Titles already measured. Retired; on the one photo the title runs x 0.147-0.385 (length 0.238) and the wave, its stripe and teal line run aft to about x 0.45 (under the wing's leading edge), not 0.35: both corrected.",
  "from": "2019-10",
